<article class="env-lemma" id="0F6A">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F6A">Lemma <span data-tag="0F6A">61.17.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. For $K \in D(S_{pro\text{-}\acute{e}tale})$ the map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  K \longrightarrow R\pi _{S, *}\pi _ S^{-1}K  \]
</div>
  <p> is an isomorphism. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because both $\pi _ S^{-1}$ and $\pi _{S, *} = i_ S^{-1}$ are exact functors and the composition $\pi _{S, *} \circ \pi _ S^{-1}$ is the identity functor. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>